# Step 5 baseline artifacts are evidence, not source.
#
# Their SHA-256 hashes are recorded in supabase/baseline/MANIFEST.md and were
# proven by the Step 5 reproduction gate. core.autocrlf is true in this
# environment, so without this rule git would normalise line endings on commit
# or checkout and silently change the bytes — turning a verified artifact into
# a different file while the manifest still claimed the old hash.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for this directory.
supabase/baseline/** -text

# The baseline migration carries 573 CR bytes, inherited from the 31 production
# function definitions that contain them. Those bytes are part of the artifact
# that was proven on a scratch project, and its SHA-256 is asserted by
# tests/migration-directory-guard.test.ts. Without this rule git normalises the
# file on commit -- measured: the blob loses all 573 CRs, becomes 955,827 bytes
# and hashes be95ddfe…, so the repository would hold a different file from the
# one that was verified.
supabase/migrations/20260821105505_baseline.sql -text
